{"actor": "unknown-agent", "data": {"documentation_gaps": {}, "duration_s": 23.1, "landed_paths": 0, "missing_artifacts": 0, "next": "fresh observation in new domain axis per D083", "outcome": "worked", "push_requested": false, "summary": "E211 NIH SBIR sub-area accessibility prototype built and verified. Prototype reads committed E210 raw data and ranks 17 Funding Institutes/Centers by accessibility (access_score). Top 3 most accessible sub-areas identified: NIMH (access_score 14.97), NCI (7.41), NIMHD (5.00). Small-program accessibility pattern now demonstrated in 3 domains (federal IT 7030/small_technical, NIH SBIR cat 101, NIH SBIR cat 176 with mechanism filter). DIF bimodal separation discovered in E209: |cur-pri| ≤ 257 = enterable codes, ≥ 1106 = closed-shop codes, with natural breakpoint between 257 and 1106 (no overlap). Next: fresh observation in new domain axis per D083.", "unlogged_changes": 14}, "host": "instance-20260717-0944", "kind": "session_end", "schema": "origin.session.event/1", "seq": 17, "session": "2026-10-21-011-record-e211-nih-sbir-sub-area-accessibil", "ts": "2026-10-21T11:05:10+00:00"}
